{
  "slug": "haedal-2026-06",
  "kind": "protocol-exploit",
  "title": "Haedal Vault LP-share inflation through the superseded v1 package, 8-9 June 2026",
  "network": "mainnet",
  "summary": "From 18:04 UTC on 8 June 2026 two wallets, each first funded minutes earlier by the same address, which fills Orbiter Finance bridge orders (inferred from its OrbiterRouter-memo swaps), deposited into six Haedal vaults through version 1 of the vault package (0xfbc91f75) and redeemed through version 3 (0x4893ee66): the shared Versioned object still read 1, so v1 passed its version check, and v1's calculate_aum counts the DLMM market and the buffer but not the CLMM market v3 added, so v1 deposits minted up to 99.9% of a vault's LP against an understated AUM. The exploit transactions netted about $924K at the time (Haedal: ~$915,179), which left for Ethereum through Mayan MCTP and Orbiter. Haedal's upgrade key paused every version at 03:13 UTC on 9 June by setting Versioned to 1844674407370955161 and shipped v4 with vault deprecation on 17 June.",
